    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0528" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 British Honduras/191</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>)<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d304-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-05">August 5, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Ronald</hi>: I have received with
                    appreciation your letter of July 31st in which you recount the steps which have
                    been taken in the various British possessions in this hemisphere to prevent the
                    smuggling of alcohol and liquor into the United States.</p>
                <p>Without commenting in detail on the action which has been taken in the various
                    colonies, I may say that we are greatly impressed with the evident desire of
                    your Government to cooperate with us and assist us in the suppression of illicit
                    traffic. I hope that we may feel free to discuss with you in an informal way
                    from time to time any problems which may arise in connection with possible
                    illicit shipments from particular localities.</p>
                <p>I desire to express to you my very deep appreciation of your helpful cooperation
                    in this matter.</p>
                <p>With renewed thanks [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgenthau Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
